ps://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-19T13:57:08Z","updated_at":"2026-02-19T13:57:08Z","body":"> I just saw the issue and thought it would be better to fix it once for every node so we dont have to hunt them down manually\r\n\r\nTo prevent such collisions in the future, we could add a check in `make_rst.py`. The names of virtual method parameters should not match keywords, global functions, or properties of the current class or its ancestors.\r\n\r\nHowever, this doesn't solve the problem if the user defines a member of the same name in a custom class. In this case, a prefix like `p_` might help.\r\n\r\n* See also #88695.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3927474606/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3945387822","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116476#issuecomment-3945387822","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/116476","id":3945387822,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rKdcu","user":{"login":"HamidRezaLS","id":144286220,"node_id":"U_kgDOCJmiDA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/144286220?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidRezaLS","html_url":"https://github.com/HamidRezaLS","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidRezaLS/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidRezaLS/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidRezaLS/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidRezaLS/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidRezaLS/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidRezaLS/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidRezaLS/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidRezaLS/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HamidRezaLS/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-23T15:21:04Z","updated_at":"2026-02-23T15:21:04Z","body":" thanks for the context @dalexeev #88695 looks like a great addition to the editor. \r\n \r\nactually these two approaches complement each other perfectly. If your PR merges, this dynamic collision check could easily be updated to read from the new `editor/naming/function_parameter_prefix` setting instead of hardcoding `\"p_\"`. so the users custom prefix handles both standard generation and dynamic collision avoidance on custom scripts.\r\n \r\n *(P.S. just pushed an amend to fix the `clang-format` tabs vs spaces failure)*","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3945387822/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]